                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Surprisingly I enjoyed playing Nicolas Eymerich - The Inquisitor - Book 1 : The Plague, albeit its shortcomings.\n\nWhat I liked:\n- The unhinged protagonist\n- The story\n- The interactions between characters and enviroment\n- It still runs great in 2026\n- The first 90% of the game that plays out in the monestary.\n\nWhat I didn't like:\n- The camera perspective in many locations. The camera pans around when you walk and many points of interest are hard to see or can only be seen from a specific angle in a location.\n- The miryriad of so called easter eggs that pull you out of the game and its worldbuilding.\n- Puzzles that have seemingly nothing to do with the game or your mission.\n- Achievements that are easy to miss, hard to aquire or absolutely nonsensical to even try to get them.\n- The last 10% the game plays out in the plague village and are literally a fever dream.\n\nAlso this game ends on a cliffhanger and the story is continued in Nicolas Eymerich The Inquisitor Book II : The Village.\n\nMy rating 6,5/10, recommended for avid adventure players.",
